## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates expertise in designing comprehensive test strategies for complex multi-tenant data protection systems, particularly focusing on dynamic policy enforcement and reliability under various failure scenarios—essential for compliance-heavy enterprise environments.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped field-level masking and policy data freshness
- Race conditions during real-time policy modifications
- Administrative rollback scenarios and data leakage risk assessment
- Cache interaction patterns and tenant churn performance optimization
- Contract testing, chaos engineering, and end-to-end resilience validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo example: contract test snippet using Pact-like syntax
const { pact } = require('pact-lang');

// Verify masked fields respect tenant-specific policies
pact({
  uponReceiving: 'request for customer data',
  withRequest: {
    method: 'GET',
    path: '/api/customers/123',
    headers: { 'X-Tenant-ID': 'tenant-A' }
  },
  willRespondWith: {
    status: 200,
    body: {
      id: '123',
      name: 'John Doe',
      // Sensitive field properly masked based on tenant policy
      ssn: '***-**-****'
    }
  }
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

Real-time, asynchronous, event-driven integrations with external partners are inherently error-prone. This question evaluates understanding of contract testing, schema evolution strategy, latency SLAs, idempotency, and resilience patterns—all critical for payment infrastructure reliability.

## Key Concepts

- Consumer-driven contracts (Pact) for multi-party API agreements
- Backward-compatible schema evolution with feature-flagged payloads
- Async webhook reliability: retries, dead-letter queues, circuit breakers
- End-to-end latency measurement with OpenTelemetry distributed tracing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pact contract for webhook payload versioning
const { Pact } = require('@pact-foundation/pact');

const provider = new Pact({
  consumer: 'fraud-gateway',
  provider: 'partner-webhook',
  cors: true,
});

describe('Partner Webhook Contract', () => {
  before(() => provider.setup());
  after(() => provider.finalize());

  it('accepts v2 schema with optional risk fields', async () => {
    await provider.addInteraction({
      state: 'partner supports v2 schema',
      uponReceiving: 'a fraud score webhook',
      withRequest: {
        method: 'POST',
        path: '/partners/123/webhook',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: {
          transactionId: 'txn_abc123',
          riskScore: 85,
          newField: 'feature-flag-value', // v2-only field
        },
      },
      willRespondWith: {
        status: 200,
        body: { received: true },
      },
    });
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
